(2207180, 299671, 2490, '<td valign="top">I think this is an extremely good image, but I''m going to abstain from voting due to my personal belief about alcohol.  No offense, I just wanted to commend you for a good image without screwing up your score unfairly.  Good luck.</td>', 'I think this is an extremely good image, but I''m going to abstain from voting due to my personal belief about alcohol.  No offense, I just wanted to commend you for a good image without screwing up your score unfairly.  Good luck.', '2006-03-07 12:30:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(2207188, 301415, 2490, '<td valign="top">Well, hmmph.  This is an excellent image, and I honestly don''t know how to score it.  It''s beautiful.  It''s a winner for technical excellence.  Great composition, perfect color, great sharpness, yadda yadda.  I just can''t see "painting with light", you know?  Did you think "make a painting by using light" and use a couple of sources, or did you somehow manage to move a light really accurately and consistently during your exposure?  This is too smooth, too perfect, and too sharp to have been done the way I think of as "painting with light".  I want to score it high and ignore the challenge, but I don''t want something of debateable nature to win the challenge - and I think this could.  Should I drop my vote because I don''t think it''s really "painting with light", or should I vote it high because it''s awesome and ignore the challenge?  Either it really deserves to win or it really doesn''t.  I''ll come down on the high side but punish you :) by a point... 9</td>', 'Well, hmmph.  This is an excellent image, and I honestly don''t know how to score it.  It''s beautiful.  It''s a winner for technical excellence.  Great composition, perfect color, great sharpness, yadda yadda.  I just can''t see "painting with light", you know?  Did you think "make a painting by using light" and use a couple of sources, or did you somehow manage to move a light really accurately and consistently during your exposure?  This is too smooth, too perfect, and too sharp to have been done the way I think of as "painting with light".  I want to score it high and ignore the challenge, but I don''t want something of debateable nature to win the challenge - and I think this could.  Should I drop my vote because I don''t think it''s really "painting with light", or should I vote it high because it''s awesome and ignore the challenge?  Either it really deserves to win or it really doesn''t.  I''ll come down on the high side but punish you :) by a point... 9', '2006-03-07 12:36:42.000000', NULL, 1),
