(2212022, 301648, 27306, '<td valign="top">I counted up: took 97 shots. These include also some practise-shots, where I used a static object instead of my daughter - it was a toy, placed about the same height as her head. I chose the very last one for submission.<br/>The most difficult part was keep the speed of the torch at a fairly constant speed, to avoid large differences in the brightness. Placing the eye and tongue was also a challenge :)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-03-08 17:06:33.</i></td>', 'I counted up: took 97 shots. These include also some practise-shots, where I used a static object instead of my daughter - it was a toy, placed about the same height as her head. I chose the very last one for submission.The most difficult part was keep the speed of the torch at a fairly constant speed, to avoid large differences in the brightness. Placing the eye and tongue was also a challenge :)', '2006-03-08 16:57:49.000000', '2006-03-08 17:06:33.000000', 0),
