(2214728, 301627, 31042, '<td valign="top">hey, i think this one looks better, and more real than your other more-photoshopped one, great job ... a little more even flashlight work would enhance it, but other than that, nicely done!<br/> <br/>Simon</td>', 'hey, i think this one looks better, and more real than your other more-photoshopped one, great job ... a little more even flashlight work would enhance it, but other than that, nicely done! Simon', '2006-03-09 15:08:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(2214747, 301265, 50695, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the wonderful comments. Unlike other people''s entries, this is not the light source, but the light being shined on a surface, in this case a door. I had a flashlight with some tape over it, which created an unusual "brush shape". Then I went right up to the door, so that for all intents and purposes I was drawing on the door with the flashlight, except that I was working blind. That was how I was able to get the variation in line width and intensity. The white lines that were mentioned were from planks in the door.<br/> <br/>John Lennon, huh? That''s big flattery. :)</td>', 'Thanks for the wonderful comments. Unlike other people''s entries, this is not the light source, but the light being shined on a surface, in this case a door. I had a flashlight with some tape over it, which created an unusual "brush shape". Then I went right up to the door, so that for all intents and purposes I was drawing on the door with the flashlight, except that I was working blind. That was how I was able to get the variation in line width and intensity. The white lines that were mentioned were from planks in the door. John Lennon, huh? That''s big flattery. :)', '2006-03-09 15:14:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(2215145, 301853, 53011, '<td valign="top">THIS IS VERY PRETTY! I REALLY LIKE IT! GOOD JOB!</td>', 'THIS IS VERY PRETTY! I REALLY LIKE IT! GOOD JOB!', '2006-03-09 17:38:40.000000', NULL, 0),
