(2226999, 299603, 14476, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>Welcome to DPC.  Your first challenge, and a terrific entry.  <br/> <br/>Now, I think you know there are a few technical issues with this image: not sharp, blown highlights, and all that.  And that is probably what our voters who hurry through images saw, and voted accordingly.<br/> <br/>BUT.<br/> <br/>It seems to me that the "technical issues" help make this picture.  Lots of interesting spots to linger, lots of glowing highlights to accentuate the fascinating vehicle you found.  Certainly your composition is splendid.  Frankly I think you captured a splendid mood, right down to the red splash.  <br/> <br/>I''m sorry you didn''t score well.  Keep ''em coming!<br/> <br/>Alice</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club  Welcome to DPC.  Your first challenge, and a terrific entry.   Now, I think you know there are a few technical issues with this image: not sharp, blown highlights, and all that.  And that is probably what our voters who hurry through images saw, and voted accordingly. BUT. It seems to me that the "technical issues" help make this picture.  Lots of interesting spots to linger, lots of glowing highlights to accentuate the fascinating vehicle you found.  Certainly your composition is splendid.  Frankly I think you captured a splendid mood, right down to the red splash.   I''m sorry you didn''t score well.  Keep ''em coming! Alice', '2006-03-14 11:20:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(2227047, 301264, 14476, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>Welcome to DPC!  You have really scaled the heights in scoring in your first two Challenges.  Keep this up and you''ll be on the front page in no time flat.<br/> <br/>This is a deceptively simple image that undoubtedly took a good deal of planning to get just right.  And get it just right you did.  You received a super score and you have left me very little, if anything, to critique.<br/> <br/>So, I shall say "Congratulations on a fine entry" and head on to the next image in the queue.<br/> <br/>I shall certainly look forward to seeing more of your work on DPC.<br/> <br/>Alice</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club  Welcome to DPC!  You have really scaled the heights in scoring in your first two Challenges.  Keep this up and you''ll be on the front page in no time flat. This is a deceptively simple image that undoubtedly took a good deal of planning to get just right.  And get it just right you did.  You received a super score and you have left me very little, if anything, to critique. So, I shall say "Congratulations on a fine entry" and head on to the next image in the queue. I shall certainly look forward to seeing more of your work on DPC. Alice', '2006-03-14 11:48:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(2227073, 301250, 14476, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>Ah, good.  An entry from the Icelandic contingent!  It''s such a beautiful island and has such nice people.<br/> <br/>Ok, on to business.  I like the composition where you fill the frame and highlight various portions of the labyrinth you have created.  It is really unfortunate that the left foreground turned out-of-focus on you.  This created a barrier that many of our hurried voters would likely not take the time to circumvent.   They would then miss all the goodies you presented for enjoyment.  <br/> <br/>That really is the only critique I have on this image.  Perhaps you did shoot this at different apertures and this was the one that suited you at the time.  I''d love to see this image at, say a f5.6.<br/> <br/>I can only wish you continued success at DPC and will look forward to seeing more of your work.<br/> <br/>Alice</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club  Ah, good.  An entry from the Icelandic contingent!  It''s such a beautiful island and has such nice people. Ok, on to business.  I like the composition where you fill the frame and highlight various portions of the labyrinth you have created.  It is really unfortunate that the left foreground turned out-of-focus on you.  This created a barrier that many of our hurried voters would likely not take the time to circumvent.   They would then miss all the goodies you presented for enjoyment.   That really is the only critique I have on this image.  Perhaps you did shoot this at different apertures and this was the one that suited you at the time.  I''d love to see this image at, say a f5.6. I can only wish you continued success at DPC and will look forward to seeing more of your work. Alice', '2006-03-14 12:00:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(2227410, 299352, 8522, '<td valign="top">Critique Club:<br/> <br/>There are some nice things about this photo... the light squiggles are quite artistic. I''m not sure the exposure is as intended though, there''s a tantalising lack of shadow detail but enough to make us want to see more of it. Is it relevant that the subject looks like they''re in a wheelchair? Is it relevant that we can see what looks like a bed? Is this person connected from their isolated lives in their bedroom by the power of the internet and a webcam? Does the light represent communication and inspiration?<br/>Please fill in the Photographer''s Comments field if you want a comment from the Critique Club.</td>', 'Critique Club: There are some nice things about this photo... the light squiggles are quite artistic. I''m not sure the exposure is as intended though, there''s a tantalising lack of shadow detail but enough to make us want to see more of it. Is it relevant that the subject looks like they''re in a wheelchair? Is it relevant that we can see what looks like a bed? Is this person connected from their isolated lives in their bedroom by the power of the internet and a webcam? Does the light represent communication and inspiration?Please fill in the Photographer''s Comments field if you want a comment from the Critique Club.', '2006-03-14 14:37:40.000000', NULL, 0),
