(5480619, 299671, 52376, '<td valign="top">Good image &amp; a great message. Not the type of photography I''m usually drawn to but I just wanted to mention to the others who commented that I think they are missing the point. Granted, everything is in the interpretation but I think this one is fairly clear. If you read the message in the artist''s comment you may understand a little better. The reason the glass is pouring back into the bottle &amp; not vice versa is to give the desired message that sometimes you have to stop, say no &amp; say you''ve had enough. If the photographer were to "flip" the image as some have suggested that point would be lost, it would be like saying "just one more shot".</td>', 'Good image & a great message. Not the type of photography I''m usually drawn to but I just wanted to mention to the others who commented that I think they are missing the point. Granted, everything is in the interpretation but I think this one is fairly clear. If you read the message in the artist''s comment you may understand a little better. The reason the glass is pouring back into the bottle & not vice versa is to give the desired message that sometimes you have to stop, say no & say you''ve had enough. If the photographer were to "flip" the image as some have suggested that point would be lost, it would be like saying "just one more shot".', '2009-05-11 12:40:31.000000', NULL, 0),
